le>Change blindness: past, present, and future</article-title><source>Trends Cogn. Sci</source><volume>9</volume><year>2005</year><fpage>16</fpage><lpage>20</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/j.tics.2004.11.006">doi:10.1016/j.tics.2004.11.006</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15639436</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Srinivasan</surname><given-names>M.V</given-names></name><name><surname>Laughlin</surname><given-names>S.B</given-names></name><name><surname>Dubs</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictive coding: a fresh view of inhibition in the retina</article-title><source>Proc. R. Soc. B</source><volume>216</volume><year>1982</year><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>459</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1098/rspb.1982.0085">doi:10.1098/rspb.1982.0085</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6129637</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stromeyer</surname><given-names>C.F</given-names></name><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence against narrow-band spatial frequency channels in human vision: detectability of frequency modulated gratings</article-title><source>Vision Res</source><volume>15</volume><year>1975</year><fpage>899</fpage><lpage>910</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1016/0042-6989(75)90229-1">doi:10.1016/0042-6989(75)90229-1</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1166623</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib43"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stevens</surname><given-names>S.S</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychophysics: introduction to its perceptual, neural, and social prospects<